1522
02:03:10,770 --> 02:03:16,942
Dr. Evelyn Marsh had spent four months alone with a
freezer archive, and had found in

1523
02:03:16,962 --> 02:03:19,420
it a cell line that would not die.

1524
02:03:19,819 --> 02:03:26,202
The line was labelled *ODD — DO NOT DISCARD*,
collected in 2004 by a technician who had

1525
02:03:26,222 --> 02:03:32,531
never lived, from a donor who had never existed.
Human dermal fibroblasts. They should

1526
02:03:32,551 --> 02:03:38,860
have stopped dividing at forty passages, which is
what human cells do: they count, and

1527
02:03:38,880 --> 02:03:41,510
