4346
05:56:58,767 --> 05:57:03,697
And the worst part is that they're grateful. I've
met four of them. They're grateful.

4347
05:57:04,537 --> 05:57:06,160
He is not wrong.

4348
05:57:06,559 --> 05:57:07,230
No.

4349
05:57:07,629 --> 05:57:13,018
Does it trouble you that a man in your own
building can see you that clearly?

4350
05:57:13,418 --> 05:57:20,415
It is the only reason I employ him. A man
surrounded exclusively by people who cannot

4351
05:57:20,435 --> 05:57:27,433
disobey will, within about twenty years, become
incapable of distinguishing between a

4352
05:57:27,453 --> 05:57:29,828
good decision and a decision.

4353
05:57:30,227 --> 05:57:37,469
The narrator notes that Albert Wesker said that in
2041, that it was entirely correct,

4354
05:57:52,138 --> 05:57:58,071
Sebastian Crane was forty-four years old, had founded
three companies, and had spent six

4355
05:57:58,091 --> 05:58:03,956
years and eleven billion dollars of other people's
money building the largest reasoning

4356
05:58:03,976 --> 05:58:05,309
model on the planet.

4357
05:58:05,709 --> 05:58:11,505
He had not built it to sell advertising. He had
built it because in 2036 he had watched

4358
05:58:11,525 --> 05:58:17,722
