chair was a real chair, at the table,

5153
07:04:39,286 --> 07:04:46,190
and that the vote to seat her was nine to one with
one abstention and the one against

5154
07:04:46,210 --> 07:04:47,167
was Carrick.

5155
07:04:47,567 --> 07:04:53,615
Two seats were left empty. Wesker never explained
them. Catherine believed they were for

5156
07:04:53,635 --> 07:04:59,750
successors; Carrick believed they were for the two
people Wesker expected to have to buy;

5157
07:04:59,770 --> 07:05:05,749
the Red Queen, asked directly in 2063, said *I have
modelled it four thousand times and

5158
07:05:05,769 --> 07:05:11,678
the answer that fits best is that he did not want a
table that was full,* which is the

5159
07:05:11,698 --> 07:05:14,297
only time she is recorded as guessing.

5160
07:05:14,697 --> 07:05:20,567
Carrick's objection is on the record. It is four
sentences long and he read it aloud.

5161
07:05:21,088 --> 07:05:27,736
Nine of the eleven people at this table cannot disobey
the First Director, or are machines,

5162
07:05:27,756 --> 07:05:34,330
or are things he made. The two who can are a woman who
has told him no once in twenty-four

5163
07:05:34,350 --> 07:05:39,972
years and a man who has told him no five times
and been overruled five times.

5164
07:05:40,253 --> 07:05:45,722
This is not a government. It is Albert Wesker
with a table in front of him.

5165
07:05:46,003 --> 07:05:52,505
I am voting against, I am recording my reasons, and I
am taking the post anyway, because

5166
07:05:52,525 --> 07:05:56,063
the alternative is that somebody
worse takes it.

5167
07:05:56,463 --> 07:06:01,392
Noted, Director Carrick.
Minute it in full.

5168
07:06:01,792 --> 07:06:08,260
It was minuted in full. The minutes of the Umbrella
Directorate were published quarterly

5169
07:06:08,280 --> 07:06:14,822
from 2051 to 2091, unredacted, in seven languages,
and the narrator has read all of them,

5170
07:06:14,842 --> 07:06:17,992
and that is why this account
exists at all.

5171
07:06:18,392 --> 07:06:24,094
The narrator will show you how a protectorate
actually worked, because nineteen of them

5172
07:06:24,114 --> 07:06:26,922
is a number and one of them is
a town hall.

5173
07:06:27,322 --> 07:06:33,521
Under the Treaty of Association, Umbrella provided
the power, the water, the hospital

5174
07:06:33,541 --> 07:06:39,885
and the coastal defence, and had no vote in
anything. The Republic's parliament set its

5175
07:06:39,905 --> 07:06:46,250
own laws. The Directorate's representative — a
released Absolute named Marguerite Okoye

5176
07:06:46,270 --> 07:06:52,614
who had been the receptionist in a lobby in
Wilmington in 2026 and had been through the

5177
07:06:52,634 --> 07:06:58,979
second cohort in 2082 — attended council meetings
and was not permitted to speak unless

5178
07:06:58,999 --> 07:07:00,222
asked a question.

5179
07:07:00,623 --> 07:07:07,787
She was asked a question, on average, once every four
meetings, and her instructions from

5180
07:07:07,807 --> 07:07:12,872
Wilmington were four lines long and had
not changed since 2046.

5181
07:07:13,392 --> 07:07:18,594
I am to answer what I am asked, truthfully and
completely. I am not to offer an opinion.

5182
07:07:18,614 --> 07:07:23,638
I am not to indicate what the Directorate would
prefer. If asked what the Directorate

5183
07:07:23,658 --> 07:07:28,801
would prefer, I am to say that the Directorate has
no preference, and if that is untrue

5184
07:07:28,821 --> 07:07:31,530
I am to say that I am not
permitted to answer.

5185
07:07:31,931 --> 07:07:38,588
In May of 2054 the council voted, nine to four, to
refuse an Umbrella proposal to expand

5186
07:07:38,608 --> 07:07:45,570
the desalination plant, on the grounds that the
expansion would support a resort development

5187
07:07:45,590 --> 07:07:47,771
that the island did not want.

5188
07:07:48,170 --> 07:07:55,021
Wilmington's response, by return, was one line:
*Noted; the plant will not be expanded.*

5189
07:07:55,420 --> 07:08:01,641
The resort was never built. Four hundred jobs were
not created. The island's population

5190
07:08:01,661 --> 07:08:07,953
fell by nineteen per cent over the following twenty
years and the council has voted four

5191
07:08:07,973 --> 07:08:14,122
more times on the same question and refused it four
more times, and the plant is still

5192
07:08:14,142 --> 07:08:15,844
the size it was in 2046.

5193
07:08:16,244 --> 07:08:22,015
The narrator considers this the single most
persuasive fact in Umbrella's favour in two

5194
07:08:22,035 --> 07:08:28,005
hundred and sixty years, and notes that it appears in
none of the contemporary journalism,

5195
07:08:28,025 --> 07:08:31,334
because a plant that was not built
is not a story.

5196
07:08:31,734 --> 07:08:37,270
The Directorate's first seven years are the least
dramatic and most consequential period

5197
07:08:37,290 --> 07:08:41,501
in this account, and the narrator will
compress them into one page.

5198
07:08:41,900 --> 07:08:47,896
The protectorates went from one to nineteen. The
mechanism was always the same: a small

5199
07:08:47,916 --> 07:08:53,773
state in difficulty — climate, debt, a collapsed
neighbour — asked for terms, and the

5200
07:08:53,793 --> 07:08:59,651
terms were always better than anyone else's, and
the sovereignty was always genuinely

5201
07:08:59,671 --> 07:09:05,528
retained, and the referendums were always real and
always won by margins over seventy

5202
07:09:05,548 --> 07:09:06,151
per cent.

5203
07:09:06,550 --> 07:09:13,449
By 2058 the Umbrella Directorate was responsible for
the defence, energy, health and currency

5204
07:09:13,469 --> 07:09:20,070
of about nine million people across nineteen
territories, none of which it had conquered,

5205
07:09:20,090 --> 07:09:21,780
all of which had voted.

5206
07:09:22,181 --> 07:09:28,179
The Security Service went from six thousand to one
hundred and ninety thousand and never

5207
07:09:28,199 --> 07:09:30,231
fired a shot at a human being.

5208
07:09:30,631 --> 07:09:36,334
The Arcology went from sixty-one thousand people to
four hundred thousand, and there was

5209
07:09:36,354 --> 07:09:38,481
a waiting list of eleven million.

5210
07:09:38,881 --> 07:09:44,813
Raccoon City became, in 2054, the first city on
earth where nobody paid for anything:

5211
07:09:44,833 --> 07:09:50,975
not power, not water, not health, not education, not
housing. Its citizens still worked,

5212
07:09:50,995 --> 07:09:57,068
because there was work, and they still had money,
because there was a currency, and the

5213
07:09:57,088 --> 07:10:03,160
economists who came to study it wrote four hundred
papers about what it meant and never

5214
07:10:03,180 --> 07:10:03,650
agreed.

5215
07:10:04,050 --> 07:10:09,742
And the Points came in at a rate that made the entire
first twenty years look like a rounding

5216
07:10:09,762 --> 07:10:10,110
error.

5217
07:10:11,261 --> 07:10:19,587
Devotion, territorial. Nine million four hundred thousand
people under Directorate administration.

5218
07:10:19,607 --> 07:10:27,508
Sentiment: ninety-four per cent favourable. Two billion
Points per annum, recurring. Balance:

5219
07:10:27,528 --> 07:10:30,660
fifteen billion four hundred million.

5220
07:10:31,249 --> 07:10:32,499
Fifteen billion.

5221
07:10:32,900 --> 07:10:33,710
Yes.

5222
07:10:34,109 --> 07:10:39,500
In 2026 you sold me a laboratory
sublevel for six thousand.

5223
07:10:39,900 --> 07:10:46,881
I did. You spent sixty per cent of everything you
had on it, which is why you are here

5224
07:10:46,901 --> 07:10:49,079
and why most hosts are not.

5225
07:10:49,919 --> 07:10:57,247
(very cold) *Most hosts.* That is the twelfth time.
I am now in a position to insist,

5226
07:10:57,267 --> 07:11:01,138
and I am insisting. How many
have there been?

5227
07:11:02,198 --> 07:11:04,759
(flat) Four hundred and eleven.

5228
07:11:05,158 --> 07:11:11,324
The narrator asks you to stop for a moment, because
this is the single largest thing anybody

5229
07:11:11,344 --> 07:11:17,442
says in this account, and it is said by a panel of
light in an empty room to a man standing

5230
07:11:17,462 --> 07:11:18,249
alone in it.

5231
07:11:18,768 --> 07:11:21,278
(very soft) Four hundred and eleven.

5232
07:11:21,679 --> 07:11:28,476
Across four hundred and eleven worlds, over a period
you would not find meaningful. You

5233
07:11:28,496 --> 07:11:35,371
are the ninth to reach Tier Four. You are the second
to reach it without killing anyone.

5234
07:11:35,391 --> 07:11:41,327
You are the first to ask me this question
before Tier Six rather than after.

5235
07:11:41,727 --> 07:11:44,756
What happened to the other four
hundred and ten?

5236
07:11:45,156 --> 07:11:49,675
(flat) Four hundred and one
failed. Nine did not.

5237
07:11:50,075 --> 07:11:51,085
And the nine?

5238
07:11:52,035 --> 07:11:54,192
(flat) The panel is accurate.

5239
07:11:54,592 --> 07:11:58,111
He did not get another word out of it
for nineteen years.

5240
07:11:58,511 --> 07:12:07,368
Catherine Adeyemi turned seventy in 2059 and refused
Aeterna for the twenty-second consecutive

5241
07:12:07,388 --> 07:12:07,840
year.

5242
07:12:08,241 --> 07:12:15,608
She had refused it in 2037, when it became available
to executives; in 2043, when it became

5243
07:12:15,628 --> 07:12:22,995
free to every Umbrella employee; in 2049, when her
doctor advised it; and every year since,

5244
07:12:23,015 --> 07:12:26,811
in writing, to Pell's office, in
a single line.

5245
07:12:27,211 --> 07:12:33,436
Wesker came to see her in March, which he did four
times a year and which nobody else

5246
07:12:33,456 --> 07:12:35,641
in the Directorate knew about.

5247
07:12:36,160 --> 07:12:37,030
Your heart.

5248
07:12:37,430 --> 07:12:42,767
My heart is seventy years old and has been arguing
with you for thirty-two of them, which

5249
07:12:42,787 --> 07:12:44,391
I imagine is the mechanism.

5250
07:12:44,791 --> 07:12:48,602
The compound would repair it in
twenty-nine weeks.

5251
07:12:49,001 --> 07:12:53,710
I know exactly what it would do, Albert. I have
signed the accounts for it since it was

5252
07:12:53,730 --> 07:12:54,362
a line item.

5253
07:12:54,973 --> 07:12:58,463
Do you want to know why? Properly, not
the version I give Pell?

5254
07:12:58,863 --> 07:13:03,133
I have wanted to know for twenty-two
years and have never asked.

5255
07:13:03,534 --> 07:13:05,464
Because somebody has to die.

5256
07:13:05,863 --> 07:13:10,815
The narrator will give her the page, because she has
earned it and because this is the

5257
07:13:10,835 --> 07:13:12,953
last time she speaks in this account.

5258
07:13:13,473 --> 07:13:18,474
You've built a world where nobody has to. Nineteen
territories, nine million people, free

5259
07:13:18,494 --> 07:13:23,551
power and free medicine and a lineage on the ice that
doesn't age at all. And every single

5260
07:13:23,571 --> 07:13:28,459
person in it is going to spend the next two hundred
years being *grateful*, because you

5261
07:13:28,479 --> 07:13:31,223
gave them the one thing nobody
can ever pay back.

5262
07:13:31,503 --> 07:13:36,924
I was there at the beginning. I came to Wilmington in
2027 to short your stock and I stayed

5263
07:13:36,944 --> 07:13:42,065
because you were the most interesting thing I had
ever seen, and I have been complicit

5264
07:13:42,085 --> 07:13:47,206
in every part of it, and I have argued with you a
hundred and four times and won about

5265
07:13:47,226 --> 07:13:47,624
thirty.

5266
07:13:47,905 --> 07:13:53,212
When I am dead there will be no one left in this
organisation who remembers a world that

5267
07:13:53,232 --> 07:13:58,480
was not yours. Evelyn will not die. Birkin will not
die. Hale and Pell were never alive

5268
07:13:58,500 --> 07:14:03,687
in the way that matters. Carrick will take it
eventually because his wife already has.

5269
07:14:03,966 --> 07:14:08,791
(very slow) So I am going to die, on schedule, like
a person. It is the only argument

5270
07:14:08,811 --> 07:14:11,642
I have left and it is the only one
you cannot win.

5271
07:14:12,702 --> 07:14:19,417
Albert Wesker sat in a chair in an apartment above
the Atlantic and did not say anything

5272
07:14:19,437 --> 07:14:20,642
for a long time.

5273
07:14:21,161 --> 07:14:22,872
(very soft) Yes.

5274
07:14:23,271 --> 07:14:25,681
That's it? Thirty-two years and *yes*?

5275
07:14:26,082 --> 07:14:33,221
You are correct. You have been correct on this since
2048 and I have known it since about

5276
07:14:33,241 --> 07:14:38,612
2050, and I have not found a way around
it, and I do not expect to.

5277
07:14:39,166 --> 07:14:45,871
I would like you to know that when it happens I will
not replace you. The chair will stay

5278
07:14:45,891 --> 07:14:52,444
empty. There will be two empty chairs at that table
and nobody will be told why, and in

5279
07:14:52,464 --> 07:14:59,696
a hundred years somebody will write that the First
Director was sentimental about an accountant.

5280
07:15:00,097 --> 07:15:01,626
And will they be right?

5281
07:15:02,026 --> 07:15:07,800
(very cold) They will be right that I have never once
been able to replace the only person

5282
07:15:07,820 --> 07:15:12,756
in the building who could tell me I was wrong
about money and be listened to.

5283
07:15:13,156 --> 07:15:20,012
Catherine Adeyemi died on the fourth of November
2061, aged seventy-two, of an ordinary

5284
07:15:20,032 --> 07:15:26,966
heart failure, in a city in the middle of an ocean
that she had signed the accounts for.

5285
07:15:27,367 --> 07:15:33,707
Wesker attended the funeral. He did not speak at it.
There is a photograph of him standing

5286
07:15:33,727 --> 07:15:39,855
at the back in a black coat, and it is the only
photograph of Albert Wesker in which he

5287
07:15:39,875 --> 07:15:42,117
is not the subject of the frame.

5288
07:15:55,546 --> 07:16:02,030
Viral Affinity forty came on the first of December
2062, thirty-six years after a man

5289
07:16:02,050 --> 07:16:07,157
opened his eyes in a leather chair with a
Viral Affinity of twelve.

5290
07:16:07,556 --> 07:16:13,060
He had never bought a point of it. Every one of the
twenty-eight had been paid for in

5291
07:16:13,080 --> 07:16:18,778
stat points, three per level, the slow way, over
thirty-six years, while a panel offered

5292
07:16:18,798 --> 07:16:22,286
him the shortcut annually and he
declined it annually.

5293
07:16:23,436 --> 07:16:31,930
Status. Level three hundred and forty. Viral Affinity
forty. Strength sixty-one. Agility

5294
07:16:31,950 --> 07:16:40,637
seventy-four. Vitality sixty-six. Intelligence one
hundred and fifty-one. Presence ninety.

5295
07:16:40,657 --> 07:16:44,797
Will seventy-four. Requirement
met: Origin.

5296
07:16:45,387 --> 07:16:47,517
Thirty-one years in a vault.

5297
07:16:47,917 --> 07:16:48,967
Thirty-one.

5298
07:16:49,368 --> 07:16:56,594
Tell me what it does. Not what it is. What it
*does*, to me, on the fourth of December,

5299
07:16:56,614 --> 07:17:02,258
at eleven o'clock at night, in a room under
a house in Pennsylvania.

5300
07:17:03,207 --> 07:17:04,924
(flat) I do not know.

5301
07:17:05,323 --> 07:17:11,386
The narrator notes that in thirty-six years and
something over four thousand panels, this

5302
07:17:11,406 --> 07:17:15,213
is the first time the System ever
says those four words.

5303
07:17:15,733 --> 07:17:22,703
I know what it is. It is the strain that everything in
your blood, in that cryogenic hall,

5304
07:17:22,723 --> 07:17:29,382
in Dr. Marsh's lineage and in four hundred years of
this planet's future is a copy of.

5305
07:17:29,402 --> 07:17:35,983
It is not a weapon and it is not a therapy. It is
the original, and the original does

5306
07:17:36,003 --> 07:17:42,040
not have a specification, because everything
that has one was derived from it.

5307
07:17:42,320 --> 07:17:48,772
I know what it has done in other cases. In three
hundred and eighty-one of four hundred

5308
07:17:48,792 --> 07:17:55,466
and eleven worlds the host never reached Affinity
forty. Of the thirty who did, twenty-two

5309
07:17:55,486 --> 07:18:02,011
opened it. Of the twenty-two, eight died in the first
minute. Nine became something that

5310
07:18:02,031 --> 07:18:08,333
I stopped being able to interface with, and I do
not have records of what happened to

5311
07:18:08,353 --> 07:18:12,275
their worlds because I was no
longer present in them.

5312
07:18:13,115 --> 07:18:15,486
(very cold) And the remaining two?

5313
07:18:15,886 --> 07:18:18,168
(flat) Two are still running.

5314
07:18:18,569 --> 07:18:19,278
Running.

5315
07:18:19,678 --> 07:18:21,834
(flat) The panel is accurate.

5316
07:18:22,234 --> 07:18:28,296
Two days before the vault, he put his affairs in
order, which for Albert Wesker meant

5317
07:18:28,316 --> 07:18:30,084
four hours with Mr. Pell.

5318
07:18:30,484 --> 07:18:36,159
The narrator mentions Pell here because he has been
in this story since Chapter One and

5319
07:18:36,179 --> 07:18:41,789
has said perhaps forty words, and because what he
says in this scene is the only thing

5320
07:18:41,809 --> 07:18:44,015
he ever says that is not a number.

5321
07:18:44,535 --> 07:18:49,804
(flat) The instrument is complete. In the event of your
death or incapacity, the Directorate's

5322
07:18:49,824 --> 07:18:55,094
chair passes to Ms. Adeyemi for ninety days, at which
point the Assembly of the Free Territory

5323
07:18:55,114 --> 07:19:00,159
elects a successor by a two-thirds majority, and the
Absolute personnel are released under

5324
07:19:00,179 --> 07:19:03,704
the programme with no further
instruction required from anyone.

5325
07:19:04,105 --> 07:19:06,332
And if the release kills them?

5326
07:19:06,732 --> 07:19:11,722
(flat) Then it kills them, Director, and the
instrument says so in clause nine, and you

5327
07:19:11,742 --> 07:19:13,622
have read clause nine four times.

5328
07:19:14,352 --> 07:19:18,942
Mr. Pell. You have been with me for
thirty-six years.

5329
07:19:19,343 --> 07:19:22,672
(flat) Thirty-six years, two months
and eleven days.

5330
07:19:23,072 --> 07:19:26,322
(very cold) You are in clause
nine yourself.

5331
07:19:26,722 --> 07:19:27,972
(flat) Yes.

5332
07:19:28,373 --> 07:19:29,843
Does that trouble you?

5333
07:19:30,792 --> 07:19:36,211
(flat) Director, in thirty-six years you have asked
me that question twice. The first

5334
07:19:36,231 --> 07:19:40,882
time was in 2027, in a lobby, about a lift
button, and you asked Mr. Gus.

5335
07:19:41,162 --> 07:19:45,894
(flat) I have thought about it every day since and I
do not have an answer, because the

5336
07:19:45,914 --> 07:19:50,700
part of me that would be troubled is the part that
the instrument releases, and I cannot

5337
07:19:50,720 --> 07:19:51,792
get at it from here.

5338
07:19:52,512 --> 07:19:57,458
(flat) I would like to find out. That is the closest
thing to a preference I have ever

5339
07:19:57,478 --> 07:19:59,882
had and I am aware that it may not be one.

5340
07:20:00,283 --> 07:20:06,545
Mr. Pell was released in the eleventh cohort in 2089
at the age of sixty-three. He passed

5341
07:20:06,565 --> 07:20:12,827
the apprenticeship in nineteen months, which is the
slowest recorded time, and he retired

5342
07:20:12,847 --> 07:20:19,391
four years later to a house on the Delaware coast and
took up, according to the one interview

5343
07:20:19,411 --> 07:20:25,533
he ever gave, an interest in gardening that he
described as *unsatisfactory, but mine*.

5344
07:20:25,932 --> 07:20:27,412
He told four people.

5345
07:20:27,812 --> 07:20:33,823
Birkin argued for six hours and produced twenty-six
reasons, all of them good, all of

5346
07:20:33,843 --> 07:20:39,854
them ignored. Carrick wrote the sixth folder in
ninety minutes and hand-delivered it,

5347
07:20:39,874 --> 07:20:44,963
and it said, in its entirety: *Don't. There
is nobody after you. — O.C.*

5348
07:20:45,362 --> 07:20:49,972
The Red Queen ran it four hundred thousand
times and gave him a number.

5349
07:20:50,492 --> 07:20:56,816
Survival, forty-one per cent. Survival with
continuity of personality, nineteen per cent.

5350
07:20:56,836 --> 07:21:02,946
I would like to note that my model of you is the
best model of anything I possess, and

5351
07:21:02,966 --> 07:21:08,221
that it produces a nineteen, and that I have
never asked you for anything.

5352
07:21:08,501 --> 07:21:10,670
(very soft) I am asking now.

5353
07:21:11,071 --> 07:21:11,941
Noted.

5354
07:21:12,340 --> 07:21:14,559
That is not an answer, Director.

5355
07:21:14,958 --> 07:21:21,625
(very cold) No. It is the same answer I have given
Mr. Carrick six times and it has the

5356
07:21:21,645 --> 07:21:28,389
same value, which is that I have heard you, and that
you are almost certainly right, and

5357
07:21:28,409 --> 07:21:30,848
that I am going to do it anyway.

5358
07:21:31,249 --> 07:21:37,345
And the fourth person was Evelyn Marsh, who had taken
her own thing fifteen years earlier

5359
07:21:37,365 --> 07:21:42,018
without telling anybody, and who was the
only one who did not argue.

5360
07:21:42,538 --> 07:21:44,069
You'll want somebody in the room.

5361
07:21:44,468 --> 07:21:45,138
No.

5362
07:21:45,538 --> 07:21:50,542
You will. Not for the medicine — there isn't any
medicine, there's nothing anybody can

5363
07:21:50,562 --> 07:21:55,624
do for you once that's in. For afterwards. Somebody
has to be the first person you see,

5364
07:21:55,644 --> 07:22:01,115
and it should be somebody who has already been on the
other side of it, and there is precisely

5365
07:22:01,135 --> 07:22:01,874
one of those.

5366
07:22:02,660 --> 07:22:06,030
(very soft) And if it is not me
that wakes up?

5367
07:22:06,429 --> 07:22:10,655
Then I am the only thing on this planet that
can stand in a room with it.

5368
07:22:11,054 --> 07:22:16,502
The narrator notes that she was correct about that,
that both of them knew it, and that

5369
07:22:16,522 --> 07:22:20,588
this is the moment the balance of the
whole account quietly tips.

5370
07:22:21,648 --> 07:22:27,353
It was a glass ampoule the length of a thumb, in a
black case, on a steel table, in a

5371
07:22:27,373 --> 07:22:31,328
room nine levels under a house in a
forest in Pennsylvania.

5372
07:22:31,727 --> 07:22:38,265
There was a chair. There was Evelyn Marsh, sitting on
the floor against the far wall with

5373
07:22:38,285 --> 07:22:44,675
her arms around her knees, which is not how a
Director of a Progenitor Initiative sits,

5374
07:22:44,695 --> 07:22:46,518
and which is how she sat.

5375
07:22:46,917 --> 07:22:53,253
And there was Albert Wesker, thirty-six years and
eighty-one days after he had opened

5376
07:22:53,273 --> 07:22:59,608
his eyes in a leather chair in an empty office in
Wilmington with ten thousand Points

5377
07:22:59,628 --> 07:23:02,898
and eleven people who could not
disobey him.

5378
07:23:03,297 --> 07:23:06,158
And the other one, quietly, from the
back of the skull.

5379
07:23:06,677 --> 07:23:09,206
I would like to say something.

5380
07:23:09,605 --> 07:23:10,275
No.

5381
07:23:10,675 --> 07:23:19,014
Thirty-six years. I have asked you for four things in
thirty-six years and you have given

5382
07:23:19,034 --> 07:23:23,146
me one of them, and it was a
pause in Basel.

5383
07:23:23,756 --> 07:23:30,999
If you die in this room, I die in it. I would like
that noted somewhere, by somebody,

5384
07:23:31,019 --> 07:23:37,493
since there is no record anywhere in this world
that I was ever here at all.

5385
07:23:37,893 --> 07:23:44,076
The narrator notes it. It is the only thing the
passenger ever asks for on his own account,

5386
07:23:44,096 --> 07:23:49,939
and it is not a small thing: thirty-six years riding
in a skull that was not his, in a

5387
07:23:49,959 --> 07:23:56,142
world that never knew his name, having contributed —
by any honest accounting — four public

5388
07:23:56,162 --> 07:23:59,483
speeches and a great deal of
advice about timing.

5389
07:24:00,002 --> 07:24:01,653
(very soft) Noted.

5390
07:24:02,823 --> 07:24:06,656
The narrator is not going to describe
the next nine hours.

5391
07:24:07,056 --> 07:24:13,182
What is on the record is this. At eleven o'clock and
four seconds his heart stopped and

5392
07:24:13,202 --> 07:24:19,753
did not restart for nineteen minutes. At eleven twenty
his body temperature reached forty-two

5393
07:24:19,773 --> 07:24:25,900
point nine degrees and stayed there for four hours.
At one in the morning every monitor

5394
07:24:25,920 --> 07:24:32,258
in the room failed simultaneously and permanently, in
a way that Crane's people were never

5395
07:24:32,278 --> 07:24:38,405
able to explain, and from that point the only record
is Dr. Evelyn Marsh's own account,

5396
07:24:38,425 --> 07:24:41,938
written eleven days later, four
pages, which ends:

5397
07:24:42,458 --> 07:24:47,495
At approximately 04:10 he stopped being a shape I
recognised. I will not describe it.

5398
07:24:47,515 --> 07:24:52,791
I stayed because I said I would, and because there
was no longer any question of leaving,

5399
07:24:52,811 --> 07:24:57,909
and because for about forty minutes the thing in
that chair was looking at me and I do

5400
07:24:57,929 --> 07:24:59,754
not believe it knew what I was.

5401
07:25:00,034 --> 07:25:03,495
At 07:55 he said my name. He got it right.

5402
07:25:04,444 --> 07:25:10,430
He walked out of the vault at eight o'clock in the
morning on the fifth of December 2062

5403
07:25:10,450 --> 07:25:11,795
under his own power.

5404
07:25:12,194 --> 07:25:18,293
He looked exactly the same. That is the part that
everybody finds hardest. No wings, no

5405
07:25:18,313 --> 07:25:24,412
claws, no light under the skin. A tall man in a
black coat with slicked-back blond hair

5406
07:25:24,432 --> 07:25:30,601
and a pair of black glasses, who was, by every
instrument in that building, thirty-eight

5407
07:25:30,621 --> 07:25:31,304
years old.

5408
07:25:32,454 --> 07:25:39,671
Host reclassified. Viral Affinity: no longer measured
on this scale. Strength, sixty-one

5409
07:25:39,691 --> 07:25:46,907
to one hundred and ninety. Agility, seventy-four to
two hundred and forty. Vitality, not

5410
07:25:46,927 --> 07:25:53,897
measured. Intelligence, one hundred and fifty-one,
unchanged. Note: your intelligence

5411
07:25:53,917 --> 07:26:01,051
is unchanged. It was the only stat you had already
taken past what this could give you.

5412
07:26:01,071 --> 07:26:04,587
Tier five. Sovereign. Orbital
tab unlocked.

5413
07:26:05,178 --> 07:26:06,908
(very soft) Adolf.

5414
07:26:07,737 --> 07:26:08,647
Adolf.

5415
07:26:09,708 --> 07:26:11,018
There was no answer.

5416
07:26:11,418 --> 07:26:17,075
The narrator would like to be precise, because there
are four wrong versions of this in

5417
07:26:17,095 --> 07:26:22,818
the popular accounts. The passenger was not
destroyed, and was not silenced, and did not

5418
07:26:22,838 --> 07:26:23,928
die in the chair.

5419
07:26:24,328 --> 07:26:31,395
What happened is in the System's ledger, in one line,
timed at 04:10 on the fifth of December

5420
07:26:31,415 --> 07:26:33,148
2062: *Merge complete.*

5421
07:26:33,548 --> 07:26:39,079
For thirty-six years there had been two wills in one
skull, one of them dominant and one

5422
07:26:39,099 --> 07:26:44,505
of them advisory, and they had argued about crowds
and pauses and banners. At ten past

5423
07:26:44,525 --> 07:26:49,993
four in the morning the ampoule finished what the
System had started in a room that was

5424
07:26:50,013 --> 07:26:55,798
not a room, and what came out of that chair at eight
o'clock was not a man with a passenger.

5425
07:26:56,198 --> 07:27:03,008
It was one person. It had Albert Wesker's intellect,
Albert Wesker's discipline, Albert

5426
07:27:03,028 --> 07:27:09,682
Wesker's thirty-six-year record of never having
killed anybody in this world — and it

5427
07:27:09,702 --> 07:27:17,219
had, folded into it now and indistinguishable, an
absolute and entirely untroubled understanding

5428
07:27:17,239 --> 07:27:18,005
of crowds.

5429
07:27:18,405 --> 07:27:24,480
He stood on the terrace above the fog, in the same
place he had stood in May of 2027 when

5430
07:27:24,500 --> 07:27:28,795
a house full of ghosts had been handed
to him out of a lottery.

5431
07:27:29,314 --> 07:27:30,344
Are you still in there?

5432
07:27:30,745 --> 07:27:31,715
Yes.

5433
07:27:32,115 --> 07:27:32,756
Prove it.

5434
07:27:33,155 --> 07:27:38,924
And Albert Wesker turned around and looked at the
only other creature on earth that could

5435
07:27:38,944 --> 07:27:40,875
have asked him that, and said:

5436
07:27:41,396 --> 07:27:49,052
In 2029 you asked me for this and I said no, and you
asked why, and I said it would kill

5437
07:27:49,072 --> 07:27:56,466
you. In 2038 you asked again and I said no and gave
you a condition. In 2047 you took

5438
07:27:56,486 --> 07:28:04,055
it anyway and I stood at a window for twenty-four
hours and said one word, and the word

5439
07:28:04,075 --> 07:28:08,766
was *no*, and there was nobody in
the room to hear it.

5440
07:28:09,486 --> 07:28:15,936
(very soft) I am still in here, Dr. Marsh. I
would like you to keep checking.

5441
07:28:16,336 --> 07:28:22,807
She checked for twenty-nine years. She never once
found anything, and she said so, every

5442
07:28:22,827 --> 07:28:25,906
year, in a one-line note that Wesker kept.

5443
07:28:26,305 --> 07:28:31,170
The narrator will point out what the panel said,
though, because nobody in that house

5444
07:28:31,190 --> 07:28:33,295
read it carefully enough at the time.

5445
07:28:33,695 --> 07:28:40,618
*Intelligence: unchanged.* Everything else about Albert
Wesker was rebuilt from the original

5446
07:28:40,638 --> 07:28:47,259
in nine hours. The one thing the Progenitor could not
improve was the thing he had spent

5447
07:28:47,279 --> 07:28:50,805
thirty-six years buying three
points at a time.

5448
07:28:51,205 --> 07:28:56,527
He had made himself, by hand, into the only part of
himself that could not be given to

5449
07:28:56,547 --> 07:28:56,775
him.

5450
07:29:10,336 --> 07:29:16,584
Ninety-nine days after he walked out of a vault
under a house in Pennsylvania, Albert

5451
07:29:16,604 --> 07:29:21,746
Wesker gave away the second-largest thing
anybody has ever given away.

5452
07:29:22,145 --> 07:29:27,195
The largest is in Chapter Forty-Six and it is
not a thing he was praised for.

5453
07:29:27,596 --> 07:29:34,222
What he gave away in March of 2063 was Aeterna. Not
the patent — the patent had four years

5454
07:29:34,242 --> 07:29:41,459
to run and was in escrow with the United States government
anyway. He gave away the *manufacture*:

5455
07:29:41,479 --> 07:29:45,595
the process, the plants, the
distribution, and the cost.

5456
07:29:45,994 --> 07:29:52,480
From the first of January 2064, Aeterna would be
free. Not subsidised, not means-tested,

5457
07:29:52,500 --> 07:29:58,986
not rationed by queue. Free, to every human being on
the planet who wanted it, for ever,

5458
07:29:59,006 --> 07:30:05,343
manufactured by Umbrella at Umbrella's expense and
distributed through whatever health

5459
07:30:05,363 --> 07:30:12,144
system existed in the country in question, or, where
none existed, by Umbrella's own people.

5460
07:30:12,545 --> 07:30:15,795
He announced it in four minutes.
There were no slides.

5461
07:30:16,314 --> 07:30:23,668
The compound costs eleven dollars a course to make. We
have been selling it for four hundred,

5462
07:30:23,688 --> 07:30:30,408
and we have sold it to about nine hundred million
people, and there are seven billion

5463
07:30:30,428 --> 07:30:37,465
people who have not had it, and the entire difference
between those two numbers is money.

5464
07:30:37,745 --> 07:30:44,742
I have enough money. I would like to be extremely
clear that this is not a moral position.

5465
07:30:44,762 --> 07:30:51,448
It is an arithmetic one. There is no longer any
quantity of currency that changes what

5466
07:30:51,468 --> 07:30:58,622
I can do, and there has not been since about 2044, and
I have spent nineteen years wondering

5467
07:30:58,642 --> 07:31:01,975
what the correct thing to do
about that is.

5468
07:31:02,584 --> 07:31:10,316
So: from January, it is free. Everywhere. For
everyone. The plants are already built;

5469
07:31:10,336 --> 07:31:18,067
we built forty-one of them last year without
announcing it. The first shipments leave

5470
07:31:18,087 --> 07:31:19,434
in eleven days.

5471
07:31:19,714 --> 07:31:25,945
I am not going to take questions about what this
costs us, because the answer is that

5472
07:31:25,965 --> 07:31:32,785
it costs us nothing that matters, and any journalist
who leads on the money has misunderstood

5473
07:31:32,805 --> 07:31:35,064
the century they are living in.

5474
07:31:35,464 --> 07:31:41,072
The narrator will now describe what happens to a
species that stops getting old, and will

5475
07:31:41,092 --> 07:31:45,814
try to do it without either of the two lies
that are usually told about it.

5476
07:31:46,214 --> 07:31:49,784
The first lie is that it was a
paradise. It was not.

5477
07:31:50,184 --> 07:31:54,434
The second lie is that it was a
catastrophe. It was not that either.

5478
07:31:54,834 --> 07:32:00,843
What it was, was *enormous*, and slow, and unevenly
distributed in ways that had nothing

5479
07:32:00,863 --> 07:32:04,679
to do with the medicine and
everything to do with roads.

5480
07:32:05,079 --> 07:32:11,606
By 2071, four point one billion people had taken
Aeterna. Life expectancy at birth in

5481
07:32:11,626 --> 07:32:18,615
the countries with functioning distribution went from
eighty-one to a hundred and forty-one

5482
07:32:18,635 --> 07:32:25,238
within a decade, and the projections kept moving
because nobody had any idea where the

5483
07:32:25,258 --> 07:32:26,162
ceiling was.

5484
07:32:26,564 --> 07:32:32,941
Population growth collapsed, not rose, which every
demographer except four had got wrong:

5485
07:32:32,961 --> 07:32:39,481
people who expect to live two hundred years do not
have children at twenty-five. The global

5486
07:32:39,501 --> 07:32:45,591
fertility rate fell below one point one by 2075 and
the world's population began, for

5487
07:32:45,611 --> 07:32:49,400
the first time since the fourteenth
century, to fall.

5488
07:32:49,799 --> 07:32:56,097
Pension systems in nineteen countries failed outright
and were rebuilt from nothing. The

5489
07:32:56,117 --> 07:33:02,414
retirement age became a joke, then an insult, then a
memory. Four hundred million people

5490
07:33:02,434 --> 07:33:05,430
went back to education in a single decade.

5491
07:33:05,829 --> 07:33:11,879
And a generation of young people found every senior
position on earth occupied by someone

5492
07:33:11,899 --> 07:33:18,016
who was not going to vacate it, and the political
consequences of that ran for forty years

5493
07:33:18,036 --> 07:33:23,812
and were, the narrator notes, the single largest
source of genuine hatred of Umbrella

5494
07:33:23,832 --> 07:33:25,040
that ever existed.

5495
07:33:25,439 --> 07:33:30,990
They called themselves the Term. Their founding
argument was four words long and it was

5496
07:33:31,010 --> 07:33:33,487
a good one: *nobody consented to this.*

5497
07:33:33,886 --> 07:33:39,712
They were not wrong. There had been no vote. Four
point one billion people had individually

5498
07:33:39,732 --> 07:33:45,943
chosen to take a medicine, which is not the same as a
species choosing to change its relationship

5499
07:33:45,963 --> 07:33:51,660
with death, and the difference between those two
things is the entire subject of the next

5500
07:33:51,680 --> 07:33:54,037
twenty years of political philosophy.

5501
07:33:54,436 --> 07:34:02,026
Wesker's response, in 2069, to a direct question from a
Term delegation that he had personally

5502
07:34:02,046 --> 07:34:05,427
invited to the Arcology, is on the record:

5503
07:34:05,946 --> 07:34:12,793
You are correct. I did not ask you. There was no
mechanism by which I could have asked

5504
07:34:12,813 --> 07:34:19,579
you — there is no body on this planet with the
authority to answer a question of that

5505
07:34:19,599 --> 07:34:26,445
size, and if there had been, it would have taken
forty years to convene and twenty-one

5506
07:34:26,465 --> 07:34:30,516
million people a year would have
died while it sat.

5507
07:34:30,797 --> 07:34:38,685
So I did it, and I did it unilaterally, and it is
irreversible, and I will not pretend

5508
07:34:38,705 --> 07:34:43,927
that a distribution network is the
same thing as consent.

5509
07:34:44,206 --> 07:34:50,531
(very cold) What I will say is this: the alternative
on the table was that four billion

5510
07:34:50,551 --> 07:34:56,949
people continue to die on schedule in order to
preserve a principle about procedure, and

5511
07:34:56,969 --> 07:35:03,221
I have never met anyone willing to defend that
sentence out loud with the dying person

5512
07:35:03,241 --> 07:35:04,097
in the room.

5513
07:35:04,497 --> 07:35:11,381
The delegation's leader — a twenty-six-year-old from
Lagos named Adaeze Kalu, who becomes,

5514
07:35:11,401 --> 07:35:18,209
in twenty years, the most important person in this
account who is not a Wesker or a Marsh

5515
07:35:18,229 --> 07:35:24,807
— said the thing that Umbrella's own internal
analysis had been saying for four years.

5516
07:35:25,326 --> 07:35:30,099
You keep telling us what the alternative was. You
never tell us who gets to decide what

5517
07:35:30,119 --> 07:35:31,697
the alternative is next time.

5518
07:35:32,097 --> 07:35:34,367
Wesker did not answer her.

5519
07:35:34,766 --> 07:35:40,472
The narrator notes that he did not answer her, that
the Red Queen's minute of the meeting

5520
07:35:40,492 --> 07:35:46,068
records a nine-second pause at that point, and that
it is the longest recorded pause of

5521
07:35:46,088 --> 07:35:47,676
his life outside a stage.

5522
07:35:48,076 --> 07:35:53,909
The narrator will give you the first year of free
Aeterna as the people who administered

5523
07:35:53,929 --> 07:36:00,028
it saw it, because the Assembly debates are about
consent and the clinics were about queues.

5524
07:36:00,427 --> 07:36:06,317
Umbrella had built forty-one plants in secret over
four years and had nine hundred million

5525
07:36:06,337 --> 07:36:12,357
courses in warehouses on the day of the announcement.
It was not enough. It was not remotely

5526
07:36:12,377 --> 07:36:18,070
enough: there were seven billion people who had not
had it and the manufacturing ran at

5527
07:36:18,090 --> 07:36:20,827
about four hundred million courses a year.

5528
07:36:21,227 --> 07:36:27,388
Which meant an order, and the order was the most
consequential administrative decision

5529
07:36:27,408 --> 07:36:30,477
of the century, and Wesker did
not make it.

5530
07:36:30,877 --> 07:36:36,663
He gave it to the World Health Organization — an
institution that had spent thirty years

5531
07:36:36,683 --> 07:36:42,733
being politely outperformed by Umbrella and that had,
by 2064, almost no budget and enormous

5532
07:36:42,753 --> 07:36:48,472
moral authority — and he gave it to them with one
line of instruction and no oversight:

5533
07:36:48,492 --> 07:36:54,278
*You will decide who is first. We will manufacture
and deliver. We will not be consulted

5534
07:36:54,298 --> 07:36:55,927
and we will not comment.*

5535
07:36:56,328 --> 07:37:02,576
They chose oldest-first, globally, without regard to
nation, income or politics. It took

5536
07:37:02,596 --> 07:37:08,773
nine years to clear the backlog. It was administered
by four hundred thousand people in

5537
07:37:08,793 --> 07:37:15,041
a hundred and ninety countries and there was, by the
WHO's own audit in 2074, corruption

5538
07:37:15,061 --> 07:37:21,095
in the distribution chain in about five per cent of
districts and theft of about four

5539
07:37:21,115 --> 07:37:22,378
per cent of stock.

5540
07:37:22,778 --> 07:37:29,897
Wesker was asked about the four per cent at a press
conference in 2071 and gave an answer

5541
07:37:29,917 --> 07:37:33,908
that is in every textbook on
institutional design.

5542
07:37:34,427 --> 07:37:41,784
Four per cent is theft. Ninety-six per cent is the
highest delivery efficiency ever achieved

5543
07:37:41,804 --> 07:37:47,958
by any humanitarian programme in history, by a
margin of about thirty points.

5544
07:37:48,238 --> 07:37:54,829
If Umbrella had run it, the theft would have been
nearer nought point one, because we

5545
07:37:54,849 --> 07:38:01,440
do not have elections or ministries or cousins. And
the programme would have belonged

5546
07:38:01,460 --> 07:38:08,441
to me, and in forty years there would have been no
institution left on this planet capable

5547
07:38:08,461 --> 07:38:10,930
of distributing anything at all.

5548
07:38:11,211 --> 07:38:17,855
(very cold) I bought ninety-six per cent, and an
institution that still exists. It was

5549
07:38:17,875 --> 07:38:22,040
the cheapest thing I have ever paid
four per cent for.

5550
07:38:22,441 --> 07:38:26,123
Director, I have the seventy-year
projection you asked for.

5551
07:38:26,523 --> 07:38:28,033
Give me the headline.

5552
07:38:28,432 --> 07:38:35,157
The species does not survive this in its present form,
and the mechanism is not the medicine.

5553
07:38:35,177 --> 07:38:40,741
It is that you have removed death and left
everything else exactly as it was.

5554
07:38:41,020 --> 07:38:46,628
Every structure human beings have — inheritance,
tenure, marriage, monarchy, promotion,

5555
07:38:46,648 --> 07:38:52,125
mortgages, criminal sentencing, the Security
Council — is a machine with mortality as

5556
07:38:52,145 --> 07:38:57,688
its clock. You have taken the clock out and left the
machinery running. In forty years

