08:48:02,487 --> 08:48:09,570
Status. Level three hundred and eighty-eight. The
requirement for Beyond is level four

6364
08:48:09,590 --> 08:48:16,589
hundred. Balance: one hundred and forty-one
billion. Four orbital habitats, forty-one

6365
08:48:16,609 --> 08:48:23,691
thousand people in orbit. Note: you are twelve
levels from a tab I have not shown you.

6366
08:48:23,711 --> 08:48:28,564
I have been waiting sixty-three years
to show you that tab.

6367
08:48:29,593 --> 08:48:33,383
(very cold) You have never once said
anything like that.

6368
08:48:33,784 --> 08:48:34,914
(flat) No.

6369
08:48:35,314 --> 08:48:39,304
You said you do not evaluate. You
said you price.

6370
08:48:40,363 --> 08:48:47,512
(flat) I have been in four hundred and eleven
worlds. Nine hosts reached this line. Two

6371
08:48:47,532 --> 08:48:54,762
are still running. The other seven opened that tab
and I am still here, which means what

6372
08:48:54,782 --> 08:48:55,504
it means.

6373
08:48:55,782 --> 08:49:02,437
(flat) I am not evaluating, Director. I am telling
you that I am interested, and that

6374
08:49:02,457 --> 08:49:07,540
this is a novel condition, and that I do
not have a price for it.

6375
08:49:07,940 --> 08:49:14,403
The narrator asks you to remember that the System
said that in April of 2089, two years

6376
08:49:14,423 --> 08:49:21,035
and one month before the end of this account, and
that Albert Wesker did not ask a single

6377
08:49:21,055 --> 08:49:22,450
follow-up question.

6378
08:49:37,520 --> 08:49:43,908
Mira Halder was thirty-nine years old in 2089 and
had been a citizen of nowhere since

6379
08:49:43,928 --> 08:49:45,490
the day she was born.

6380
08:49:45,891 --> 08:49:52,097
The narrator introduced her in Chapter Twenty-Nine,
in one line, as the first child born

6381
08:49:52,117 --> 08:49:58,183
in the Arcology: a Bangladeshi structural engineer
and a Peruvian marine biologist who

6382
08:49:58,203 --> 08:50:02,640
had met in a canteen, and a hospital in
the middle of an ocean.

6383
08:50:03,041 --> 08:50:09,075
This chapter is hers, and it is here because
everything else in this account is told from

6384
08:50:09,095 --> 08:50:14,858
inside the room where the decisions are made, and
because a story told only from that

6385
08:50:14,878 --> 08:50:15,810
room is a lie.

6386
08:50:16,211 --> 08:50:21,461
What it is like to be an Umbrella citizen,
in 2089, from the inside:

6387
08:50:21,861 --> 08:50:27,964
You have never paid for anything. Not power, not
water, not medicine, not your education,

6388
08:50:27,984 --> 08:50:33,949
not the apartment you live in. You have a currency
and you use it for the things people

6389
08:50:33,969 --> 08:50:39,866
use currency for — a better coffee, a boat, a
holiday on an actual continent — but the

6390
08:50:39,886 --> 08:50:42,549
floor beneath you has never once moved.

6391
08:50:42,949 --> 08:50:48,571
You are thirty-nine and you look twenty-six, because
you have been on Aeterna since you

6392
08:50:48,591 --> 08:50:54,213
were eleven, along with everyone you know. Your
parents are seventy-one and look forty.

6393
08:50:54,233 --> 08:50:59,919
You have met exactly four people in your life who
have died, and three of them chose to.

6394
08:51:00,320 --> 08:51:06,333
You have voted in nineteen elections for the Arcology's
assembly, which controls the schools,

6395
08:51:06,353 --> 08:51:12,042
the housing, the ports, the courts and about nine per
cent of the budget. You have never

6396
08:51:12,062 --> 08:51:17,622
voted for a First Director and neither has anybody
else. The assembly has twice passed

6397
08:51:17,642 --> 08:51:23,591
resolutions asking for that to change, and both times
the Directorate has replied, politely,

6398
08:51:23,611 --> 08:51:25,797
that the question is under review.

6399
08:51:26,198 --> 08:51:29,078
It has been under review since 2064.

6400
08:51:29,597 --> 08:51:34,708
I want to be careful how I say this, because
everybody from outside wants me to either

6401
08:51:34,728 --> 08:51:38,168
denounce him or thank him, and I'm not
going to do either.

6402
08:51:38,448 --> 08:51:43,749
He is the reason my mother is alive. She had a cardiac
thing at forty-four and the hospital

6403
08:51:43,769 --> 08:51:48,720
here fixed it in an afternoon and it cost nobody
anything. He's the reason I was born

6404
08:51:48,740 --> 08:51:53,749
in a city that shouldn't exist, and the reason I've
got a job building the second one,

6405
08:51:53,769 --> 08:51:56,497
and the reason I'll probably see
the year 2300.

6406
08:51:57,108 --> 08:52:02,299
And I have never once been asked whether I wanted
any of it. Not once, in thirty-nine

6407
08:52:02,319 --> 08:52:06,897
years, about anything that mattered. We get to
vote on the ferry timetable.

6408
08:52:07,297 --> 08:52:13,865
She was, in 2089, the chief structures engineer on the
Arcology's second platform, a hundred

6409
08:52:13,885 --> 08:52:20,094
and forty kilometres south, which was being built
the slow way — with contractors, with

6410
08:52:20,114 --> 08:52:26,251
steel, over twenty-four years — because the assembly
had asked for it to be built that

6411
08:52:26,271 --> 08:52:30,547
way and the Directorate had, to
everyone's surprise, agreed.

6412
08:52:31,068 --> 08:52:35,984
That's the thing people outside don't understand about
the argument here. We're not oppressed.

6413
08:52:36,004 --> 08:52:40,710
Nobody's got a boot on us. It's that we're
*comfortable*, permanently, and we didn't build

6414
08:52:40,730 --> 08:52:45,279
it, and we can't lose it, and there's nothing any of
us can ever do that will matter as

6415
08:52:45,299 --> 08:52:47,538
much as one decision he makes
on a Tuesday.

6416
08:52:47,818 --> 08:52:52,634
(very slow) Do you know what the suicide rate is in
the Free Territory? It's four times

6417
08:52:52,654 --> 08:52:57,414
the world average, and it's all people between
thirty and sixty, and the Directorate's

6418
08:52:57,434 --> 08:53:01,028
own report says the cause is what it
calls *consequence deficit*.

6419
08:53:01,307 --> 08:53:03,337
We call it the Tuesday problem.

6420
08:53:03,737 --> 08:53:09,089
The narrator will give you one evening, because the
Assembly debates are on the record

6421
08:53:09,109 --> 08:53:10,587
and the dinners are not.

6422
08:53:10,987 --> 08:53:16,737
Mira Halder's parents were seventy-one and
sixty-nine and looked forty. Her father had

6423
08:53:16,757 --> 08:53:22,775
built the platform's second water plant; her mother
had catalogued the Atlantic's midwater

6424
08:53:22,795 --> 08:53:28,745
fish for thirty years and had four hundred papers and
no position, because there had been

6425
08:53:28,765 --> 08:53:31,093
no positions for twenty-four years.

6426
08:53:31,612 --> 08:53:35,402
I'm not complaining. I want that
understood before I say the rest.

6427
08:53:35,682 --> 08:53:41,063
I came here in 2049 from a town outside Lima that had
four hours of power a day. My daughter

6428
08:53:41,083 --> 08:53:46,171
has never been hungry, never been ill, and will
probably see the year 2300. If somebody

6429
08:53:46,191 --> 08:53:50,632
had offered me this at twenty-four I would have
run across the ocean for it.

6430
08:53:51,242 --> 08:53:55,347
(very slow) But I have been the person who
catalogues the fish for thirty years, and I

6431
08:53:55,367 --> 08:53:59,424
will be the person who catalogues the fish for
another two hundred, because the woman

6432
08:53:59,444 --> 08:54:03,549
above me is eighty-one and looks thirty-five and is
not going anywhere, and neither is

6433
08:54:03,569 --> 08:54:04,413
the man above her.

6434
08:54:04,812 --> 08:54:05,562
Mum.

6435
08:54:05,963 --> 08:54:10,894
I am not sad, Mira. I am simply telling you what the
arithmetic is, because your generation

6436
08:54:10,914 --> 08:54:15,030
keeps calling it a mood and it is not a mood.
It is a *queue* with no front.

6437
08:54:15,430 --> 08:54:21,532
The Directorate's own study of the Free Territory,
commissioned in 2086 and published

6438
08:54:21,552 --> 08:54:27,941
in 2088, put it in a sentence that the Assembly
quoted twenty-three times in one session:

6439
08:54:27,961 --> 08:54:34,279
*The territory has abolished every form of scarcity
except one, and the exception is the

6440
08:54:34,299 --> 08:54:36,656
scarcity of anything left to do.*

6441
08:54:37,055 --> 08:54:43,615
On the nineteenth of September 2089 the Arcology
Assembly debated a motion, tabled by

6442
08:54:43,635 --> 08:54:48,956
Mira Halder and eleven others, entitled *On
the Question of Consent.*

6443
08:54:49,355 --> 08:54:55,643
It asked for four things: an elected First Director;
a right of the territories to amend

6444
08:54:55,663 --> 08:55:01,807
the Directorate's charter; the publication of the
System's existence, whatever it was,

6445
08:55:01,827 --> 08:55:04,315
in plain language; and a timetable.

6446
08:55:04,716 --> 08:55:10,796
It is the single most important document produced by
anyone in this account who is not

6447
08:55:10,816 --> 08:55:16,896
Albert Wesker, and it passed the Assembly by three
hundred and fourteen votes to nine.

6448
08:55:17,295 --> 08:55:23,888
He came to answer it himself, eleven days later, which
nobody expected, and he took questions

6449
08:55:23,908 --> 08:55:26,945
for four hours, which nobody
had ever seen.

6450
08:55:27,466 --> 08:55:32,805
Director. My motion asks for a timetable. Not a
promise, not a review — a date. Will you

6451
08:55:32,825 --> 08:55:33,535
give us one?

6452
08:55:34,485 --> 08:55:35,156
No.

6453
08:55:35,555 --> 08:55:41,006
Then I'd like you to explain why to four hundred
thousand people, rather than to a committee.

6454
08:55:41,406 --> 08:55:46,336
Because an elected First Director
cannot hold what I hold.

6455
08:55:46,615 --> 08:55:53,384
I want to be very precise, because this is the
answer to everything you have asked and

6456
08:55:53,404 --> 08:56:00,726
you are entitled to the real version. It is not that an
elected person would be less capable.

6457
08:56:00,746 --> 08:56:07,436
It is that there are four hundred thousand human
beings alive today who cannot refuse

6458
08:56:07,456 --> 08:56:14,225
an instruction from me, and nine years ago twelve
governments proved what happens when

6459
08:56:14,245 --> 08:56:17,146
somebody else tries to give them one.

6460
08:56:17,425 --> 08:56:24,352
The release programme is at seventeen per cent. When
it reaches one hundred — and it will,

6461
08:56:24,372 --> 08:56:31,068
and I have committed to it in a treaty that a
tribunal I do not control enforces — then

6462
08:56:31,088 --> 08:56:37,783
the thing I hold becomes a thing that can be handed
over, and on that day you may elect

6463
08:56:37,803 --> 08:56:39,095
whoever you like.

6464
08:56:39,495 --> 08:56:40,785
That's ninety years.

6465
08:56:41,185 --> 08:56:43,576
Sixty-one, on the current rate.

6466
08:56:43,975 --> 08:56:46,225
(very slow) I'll be a hundred years old.

6467
08:56:46,625 --> 08:56:53,417
You will be a hundred years old and you will look
thirty, and you will still be building

6468
08:56:53,437 --> 08:57:00,228
things, and you will be at that election. That is the
difference between your generation

6469
08:57:00,248 --> 08:57:06,962
and every generation that came before you, and it is
the reason your argument is better

6470
08:57:06,982 --> 08:57:11,915
than any argument anybody made in the
first sixty years of this.

6471
08:57:12,756 --> 08:57:15,446
That's not an answer to the
Tuesday problem.

6472
08:57:15,846 --> 08:57:21,331
The narrator notes that the hall went quiet, and
that the Red Queen's minute records a

6473
08:57:21,351 --> 08:57:26,196
pause of eleven seconds, and that it is the
last long pause in this account.

6474
08:57:26,716 --> 08:57:29,366
(very slow) No. It is not.

6475
08:57:29,646 --> 08:57:36,895
I have read your report. I read it in July.
*Consequence deficit* is the correct diagnosis

6476
08:57:36,915 --> 08:57:43,760
and it was written by your own people, not mine,
and the Directorate has no treatment

6477
08:57:43,780 --> 08:57:47,476
for it because the disease is
the Directorate.

6478
08:57:47,756 --> 08:57:54,611
So I am going to give you the only thing I have ever
been able to give anybody that was

6479
08:57:54,631 --> 08:58:01,646
worth having, which is not safety, and is not
medicine, and is certainly not an election.

6480
08:58:02,255 --> 08:58:08,797
(very cold) In twenty-four years there will be a
shipyard in orbit, and after that there

6481
08:58:08,817 --> 08:58:15,284
will be places to go that nobody has built yet, and
no floor beneath anybody, and every

6482
08:58:15,304 --> 08:58:21,026
single one of them will be somewhere I have
never been and cannot administer.

6483
08:58:21,306 --> 08:58:27,978
You want consequence, Ms. Halder. I cannot vote one
into existence for you. I can only

6484
08:58:27,998 --> 08:58:34,981
open a door that has a great deal of nothing on the
other side of it, and let four hundred

6485
08:58:35,001 --> 08:58:42,062
thousand comfortable people decide whether they are
the kind of creature that walks through

6486
08:58:42,082 --> 08:58:42,296
it.

6487
08:58:42,696 --> 08:58:49,071
Mira Halder was, the narrator records, the fourth
human being to be recruited by Albert

6488
08:58:49,091 --> 08:58:55,466
Wesker in a single conversation, and the only one of
the four who never worked for him.

6489
08:58:55,985 --> 08:58:58,336
Then I want first refusal on the hull.

6490
08:58:59,176 --> 08:59:01,406
(very soft) On which hull?

6491
08:59:01,806 --> 08:59:06,986
The first one. Whatever it is. I'm a structures
engineer, I've built a city in an ocean,

6492
08:59:07,006 --> 08:59:12,127
and if you're going to open a frontier to solve a
philosophical problem you've created,

6493
08:59:12,147 --> 08:59:15,495
then somebody from the problem should
be holding the pen.

6494
08:59:16,446 --> 08:59:23,592
There is no recording of Albert Wesker laughing. The
narrator has said so twice in this

6495
08:59:23,612 --> 08:59:30,593
account: once in a dark office in 2027 when a
lottery gave him a monster, and once in

6496
08:59:30,613 --> 08:59:32,076
a library in 2031.

6497
08:59:32,475 --> 08:59:39,039
The Assembly's minute of the thirtieth of September 2089
records, in the clerk's own handwriting,

6498
08:59:39,059 --> 08:59:44,876
at four hours and twenty-one minutes into the
session: *The First Director appeared to

6499
08:59:44,896 --> 08:59:45,622
be amused.*

6500
08:59:46,143 --> 08:59:52,744
Ms. Halder, you may have the pen. You will find it
is extremely heavy and that nobody

6501
08:59:52,764 --> 08:59:53,913
will thank you.

6502
09:00:10,437 --> 09:00:16,895
Level four hundred came on the nineteenth of March
2090, sixty-three years and six months

6503
09:00:16,915 --> 09:00:23,227
after a man woke up at Level One with ten thousand
Points and eleven people downstairs.

6504
09:00:24,377 --> 09:00:27,927
Level four hundred. New tab. Beyond.

6505
09:00:28,517 --> 09:00:34,441
He opened it alone, at midnight, in an empty chamber
with eleven chairs and two of them

6506
09:00:34,461 --> 09:00:35,739
permanently vacant.

6507
09:00:36,888 --> 09:00:44,407
Beyond. Void-capable hull pattern, four kilometre
class: nine billion. Orbital Dock: ten

6508
09:00:44,427 --> 09:00:52,031
billion. Reaction-free drive geometry: forty billion.
Immunity to vacuum, short exposure:

6509
09:00:52,051 --> 09:00:59,313
nine hundred million. Immunity to hard radiation:
two billion. Void-adapted personnel

6510
09:00:59,333 --> 09:01:07,023
line: six billion. Deep system habitat for four
hundred thousand: eleven billion. Balance:

6511
09:01:07,043 --> 09:01:09,678
one hundred and ninety billion.

6512
09:01:10,269 --> 09:01:16,098
He read it for two hours, and then he asked the
question that he had been saving since

6513
09:01:16,118 --> 09:01:16,439
2031.

6514
09:01:16,958 --> 09:01:22,148
Reaction-free drive geometry.
Explain that item.

6515
09:01:22,549 --> 09:01:30,158
It is a hull geometry and a set of field parameters.
Applied correctly, a vessel changes

6516
09:01:30,178 --> 09:01:32,933
velocity without expelling mass.

6517
09:01:33,332 --> 09:01:36,062
(very cold) That is not possible.

6518
09:01:36,463 --> 09:01:43,662
(flat) It is not possible on the physics your
species has. It is a commonplace on the

6519
09:01:43,682 --> 09:01:51,392
physics that four hundred and eleven worlds have
arrived at independently, and your species

6520
09:01:51,412 --> 09:01:58,951
is approximately ninety years from the relevant
result, and I am selling you those ninety

6521
09:01:58,971 --> 09:02:01,585
years for forty billion Points.

6522
09:02:02,425 --> 09:02:04,095
Why is it in a shop?

6523
09:02:04,494 --> 09:02:06,150
Because you can afford it.

6524
09:02:06,550 --> 09:02:13,846
That is not what I asked and you know precisely
what I asked. Everything in every tab

6525
09:02:13,866 --> 09:02:21,162
you have ever shown me has been a thing a
corporation could conceivably have built. A

6526
09:02:21,182 --> 09:02:28,565
plant. A tower. A soldier. A city — and even the
city was concrete and people, and the

6527
09:02:28,585 --> 09:02:35,968
paperwork was the only miracle. This is not that.
This is a piece of physics that does

6528
09:02:35,988 --> 09:02:38,119
not exist on this planet.

6529
09:02:39,180 --> 09:02:40,305
(flat) Yes.

6530
09:02:40,706 --> 09:02:46,599
(very cold) Then answer the question I have asked
you four hundred times in sixty-three

6531
09:02:46,619 --> 09:02:51,696
