The four hundred and eleven thousand died because a
settlement of ninety thousand people

7168
09:58:33,172 --> 09:58:38,847
cannot be moved in four hundred days with nineteen
hulls, because the hulls had to come

7169
09:58:38,867 --> 09:58:44,673
from somewhere, and because the Assembly's evacuation
committee had to decide, in public,

7170
09:58:44,693 --> 09:58:48,928
with the transcripts published, which
settlements got them first.

7171
09:58:49,328 --> 09:58:57,221
It sat for eleven years. Its chair, a woman from Ochoa
named Iyabo Adeyemi-Sun, aged forty-four,

7172
09:58:57,241 --> 09:59:03,981
took the job because nobody else would and never
held another position afterwards.

7173
09:59:04,501 --> 09:59:08,670
We had nineteen hulls and four hundred days and
ninety thousand people at Tanager and

7174
09:59:08,690 --> 09:59:12,860
sixty thousand at the Reach and the numbers do not
work. They have never once worked.

7175
09:59:12,880 --> 09:59:17,100
I have been doing this for six years and the numbers
have not worked for a single week

7176
09:59:17,120 --> 09:59:17,396
of it.

7177
09:59:17,676 --> 09:59:22,919
The Director asked for a wider perimeter in 2168 —
pull everyone from the outer seven

7178
09:59:22,939 --> 09:59:28,491
systems now, before they are announced, at enormous
cost, on the assumption that the Choir

7179
09:59:28,511 --> 09:59:30,597
will reach all of them eventually.

7180
09:59:30,876 --> 09:59:35,471
(very slow) I voted against. Four of us voted against.
We were wrong, and sixty-one thousand

7181
09:59:35,491 --> 09:59:39,885
people died who would not have, and I have to say
that sentence at every hearing for the

7182
09:59:39,905 --> 09:59:43,547
rest of my life and I have decided that I
will say it plainly every time.

7183
09:59:44,267 --> 09:59:48,544
I would vote the same way again, and I want that on
the record too, because at the time

7184
09:59:48,564 --> 09:59:52,743
there were four hundred thousand people in the
inner systems who would have had to be

7185
09:59:52,763 --> 09:59:57,091
told that we were spending their hulls on a
prediction by a man who has been right about

7186
09:59:57,111 --> 10:00:01,290
everything for a hundred and forty years and who
nobody is allowed to simply obey any

7187
10:00:01,310 --> 10:00:01,537
more.

7188
10:00:01,816 --> 10:00:06,386
(very slow) That is what he built. He built a world
where being right is not enough. Most

7189
10:00:06,406 --> 10:00:10,872
days I think it is the finest thing anybody has ever
done and on the other days I count

7190
10:00:10,892 --> 10:00:12,006
to sixty-one thousand.

7191
10:00:12,407 --> 10:00:15,477
The Choir came anyway. Doctrine
is doctrine.

7192
10:00:15,877 --> 10:00:22,425
The narrator will describe the war of the edges in one
page, because it is the only shooting

7193
10:00:22,445 --> 10:00:27,067
war in this account and because Albert
Wesker did not command it.

7194
10:00:27,466 --> 10:00:32,544
It was fought by the Assembly's defence council,
under a doctrine written in 2144 by a

7195
10:00:32,564 --> 10:00:37,702
committee, and executed by admirals who had been
colonial engineers. It lasted fourteen

7196
10:00:37,722 --> 10:00:42,800
years. It was fought at the edges, as the Choir had
promised, and the Choir kept every

7197
10:00:42,820 --> 10:00:48,075
single one of its undertakings, because it has never
in eleven thousand years told a lie.

7198
10:00:48,475 --> 10:00:55,398
Human losses: four hundred and eleven thousand dead at
nine settlements, all of them evacuated

7199
10:00:55,418 --> 10:01:00,126
too slowly, none of them targeted after
evacuation was complete.

7200
10:01:00,526 --> 10:01:06,308
The Choir stopped four times in fourteen years,
unilaterally, each time for about nine

7201
10:01:06,328 --> 10:01:12,111
months, each time while it *listened again* — which
is in its doctrine, which no other

7202
10:01:12,131 --> 10:01:18,183
species had ever survived long enough to trigger, and
which it had not performed in eleven

7203
10:01:18,203 --> 10:01:19,196
thousand years.

7204
10:01:19,595 --> 10:01:25,856
And in 2181, at a system with no name at the edge of
the sphere, a Choir hierarch stood

7205
10:01:25,876 --> 10:01:32,498
in a human assembly hall that had been built out of a
cargo module, in front of four hundred

7206
10:01:32,518 --> 10:01:38,635
delegates from nine worlds who had been arguing
about evacuation quotas for six days,

7207
10:01:38,655 --> 10:01:41,955
and listened to them do it for
nineteen hours.

7208
10:01:43,026 --> 10:01:45,233
(very slow) We were mistaken.

7209
10:01:45,513 --> 10:01:50,419
There is a note. It is not where any of our doctrine
instructed us to listen, and it is

7210
10:01:50,439 --> 10:01:55,402
not in anything you hold, and it is not in any of
your works. It is in the disagreement,

7211
10:01:55,422 --> 10:02:00,499
which does not resolve, and which we had classified as
disorder for eleven thousand years.

7212
10:02:00,778 --> 10:02:05,565
(very slow) We have ended three species. We will now
go and be quiet for a very long time,

7213
10:02:05,585 --> 10:02:10,159
and consider what we have done, and we ask nothing
of you, because we are not entitled

7214
10:02:10,179 --> 10:02:10,532
to ask.

7215
10:02:10,932 --> 10:02:18,386
The Choir of Ashen Light withdrew from the human
sphere in 2181 and has not been heard

7216
10:02:18,406 --> 10:02:26,207
from since. Its last transmission was the eleven-word
answer of 2166, repeated once, which

7217
10:02:26,227 --> 10:02:33,767
the Compact's xenologists believe was an apology and
which nobody has ever been able to

7218
10:02:33,787 --> 10:02:34,462
confirm.

7219
10:02:34,863 --> 10:02:41,703
Albert Wesker was one hundred and fifty-five years
old and had not left the solar system

7220
10:02:41,723 --> 10:02:42,950
in thirty years.

7221
10:02:43,350 --> 10:02:49,535
He had not commanded a fleet, drafted the answer, or
spoken in the Assembly since 2161.

7222
10:02:49,555 --> 10:02:55,669
He had watched a fourteen-year war from an orbital
station and read the casualty lists

7223
10:02:55,689 --> 10:03:02,159
every morning, four hundred and eleven thousand names
over fourteen years, and the narrator

7224
10:03:02,179 --> 10:03:08,293
notes that he read all of them, and that the Red
Queen's log records the time he spent

7225
10:03:08,313 --> 10:03:08,720
on it.

7226
10:03:09,870 --> 10:03:17,339
Event: the Choir withdraws. Four hundred and eleven
thousand human dead. Attributable

7227
10:03:17,359 --> 10:03:25,181
to your decisions: zero. Attributable to decisions
you opposed: sixty-one thousand. Note:

7228
10:03:25,201 --> 10:03:32,758
you argued for a wider evacuation perimeter in
twenty one sixty-eight and the Assembly

7229
10:03:32,778 --> 10:03:35,841
voted you down. Note: you complied.

7230
10:03:37,091 --> 10:03:43,221
(very soft) Sixty-one thousand people died
because I did what I was told.

7231
10:03:43,622 --> 10:03:44,748
(flat) Yes.

7232
10:03:45,148 --> 10:03:46,199
Was I right?

7233
10:03:46,599 --> 10:03:47,724
(flat) Yes.

7234
10:03:48,675 --> 10:03:51,205
(very cold) Then say the rest of it.

7235
10:03:51,604 --> 10:03:59,409
(flat) In four hundred and eleven worlds, this is the
ninth occasion on which a host has

7236
10:03:59,429 --> 10:04:07,144
been overruled by a body he created and complied
against his own judgement at a cost in

7237
10:04:07,164 --> 10:04:07,677
lives.

7238
10:04:07,957 --> 10:04:14,365
(flat) On the other eight occasions the host
dissolved the body within the year.

7239
10:04:14,766 --> 10:04:20,592
The narrator records that Albert Wesker stood at a
window above the Earth for some time,

7240
10:04:20,612 --> 10:04:26,240
and that what he said was not to the System, and
that the Red Queen logged it because

7241
10:04:26,260 --> 10:04:29,496
she logged everything, and that
it is four words.

7242
10:04:43,605 --> 10:04:49,565
The Myriad has no name for itself, no government,
no doctrine, no art and no history,

7243
10:04:49,585 --> 10:04:55,825
and it has been at war with everything it has ever
met for somewhere between four hundred

7244
10:04:55,845 --> 10:04:58,709
thousand and nine hundred thousand years.

7245
10:04:59,109 --> 10:04:59,504
It is a hive. That word is wrong in nine ways and the
human record has never found a better

7246
10:04:59,524 --> 10:04:59,901
one. It is not a species with a queen; it is a
single distributed organism of somewhere

7247
10:04:59,921 --> 10:05:00,302
over four hundred trillion bodies, occupying eleven
hundred systems, that grows into any

7248
10:05:00,322 --> 10:05:00,717
volume it is not prevented from entering, and that has
never once in its recorded existence

7249
10:05:00,737 --> 10:05:00,817
responded to a signal.

7250
10:05:01,217 --> 10:05:06,927
The Compact has traded with everything in nine
hundred light years except the Myriad.

7251
10:05:06,947 --> 10:05:12,925
The Veth have fought it for ninety thousand years and
hold their border with four hundred

7252
10:05:12,945 --> 10:05:18,856
thousand ships. The Choir declared it noise before
the Earth had oxygen and has not been

7253
10:05:18,876 --> 10:05:19,867
able to end it.

7254
10:05:20,268 --> 10:05:28,036
It reached the human sphere in 2194, at a mining
system called the Kelpie Reach, with

7255
10:05:28,056 --> 10:05:33,717
twenty-seven thousand bodies, and ate
the system in nine days.

7256
10:05:34,117 --> 10:05:40,656
Human dead: four thousand one hundred. There was no
evacuation because there was no warning

7257
10:05:40,676 --> 10:05:46,567
and no demand and no negotiation, because there is
nobody there to negotiate with.

7258
10:05:46,965 --> 10:05:52,390
And the narrator will tell you plainly what that did
to a species that had spent forty

7259
10:05:52,410 --> 10:05:55,366
years learning to argue: it
broke the argument.

7260
10:05:55,765 --> 10:06:01,768
Within four months the Human Assembly had voted, by
three hundred and eighty-one to thirty,

7261
10:06:01,788 --> 10:06:07,526
to place the defence of the sphere under a single
unified command with emergency powers

7262
10:06:07,546 --> 10:06:13,349
— the exact instrument it had spent seventy years
refusing to create — and to offer that

7263
10:06:13,369 --> 10:06:17,055
command to the one person alive who
had fought anything.

7264
10:06:17,456 --> 10:06:18,526
He refused.

7265
10:06:19,045 --> 10:06:21,775
Director, four thousand one
hundred people —

7266
10:06:22,176 --> 10:06:28,699
(very cold) I am aware of the number. I have read
the names, as I read the four hundred

7267
10:06:28,719 --> 10:06:34,566
and eleven thousand names of the Choir war,
every morning, for fourteen years.

7268
10:06:34,846 --> 10:06:41,843
I am refusing because this Assembly is about to hand
a hundred and sixty-eight years of

7269
10:06:41,863 --> 10:06:48,700
work back to the man it took it from, in four
months, out of fear, and because I have

7270
10:06:48,720 --> 10:06:55,717
spent seventy years of my life making it impossible
for one person to hold this species

7271
10:06:55,737 --> 10:07:02,816
and I am not going to undo it in an afternoon because
something frightening has arrived.

7272
10:07:03,215 --> 10:07:06,306
And if the Myriad takes another system?

7273
10:07:06,706 --> 10:07:13,095
(very cold) Then it takes another system, and you
will have to fight it as what you are,

7274
10:07:13,115 --> 10:07:19,431
which is twelve billion people and four hundred
worlds and an argument. I will fight in

7275
10:07:19,451 --> 10:07:25,622
it. I will take any command this Assembly gives me
that has a term limit, a reporting

7276
10:07:25,642 --> 10:07:31,885
line and a review. I will not take emergency powers,
and if you vote them to me I will

7277
10:07:31,905 --> 10:07:38,076
decline them in public, on the record, and that
will be worse for you than if you had

7278
10:07:38,096 --> 10:07:39,095
never offered.

7279
10:07:40,046 --> 10:07:46,151
The narrator notes that the Assembly voted the
powers anyway, that he declined them in

7280
10:07:46,171 --> 10:07:52,349
public on the record, and that the resulting
constitutional crisis lasted eleven months

7281
10:07:52,369 --> 10:07:55,056
while the Myriad ate two more systems.

7282
10:07:55,456 --> 10:08:02,344
Nine thousand more people died in those eleven
months. The Assembly's own inquiry in 2203

7283
10:08:02,364 --> 10:08:09,098
concluded that a unified command in 2194 would have
saved most of them, and that Albert

7284
10:08:09,118 --> 10:08:15,696
Wesker's refusal was the correct decision, and the
narrator has read all four hundred

7285
10:08:15,716 --> 10:08:22,604
pages of that inquiry and has never been able to
decide whether the two findings can both

7286
10:08:22,624 --> 10:08:23,225
be true.

7287
10:08:23,625 --> 10:08:29,404
The war that followed lasted sixteen years and was
commanded by a rotating council of

7288
10:08:29,424 --> 10:08:35,476
four admirals with fixed terms, which every
professional in nine hundred light years said

7289
10:08:35,496 --> 10:08:40,115
was insane and which worked for reasons
that are still argued about.

7290
10:08:40,516 --> 10:08:43,046
Human losses: nineteen thousand.

7291
10:08:43,445 --> 10:08:49,936
Myriad losses: unknowable, because it does not have
units and does not retreat, and because

7292
10:08:49,956 --> 10:08:53,586
the word *loss* assumes something
that can be lost.

7293
10:08:53,986 --> 10:09:00,578
The frontier held. It did not advance. In sixteen
years the Myriad took nothing after

7294
10:09:00,598 --> 10:09:07,269
the eleventh month and the human sphere took nothing
at all, and by 2205 the thing had

7295
10:09:07,289 --> 10:09:14,038
become what the Veth had had for ninety thousand
years: a border, permanent, expensive,

7296
10:09:14,058 --> 10:09:14,816
and quiet.

7297
10:09:15,216 --> 10:09:21,562
And Albert Wesker fought in it, personally, which is
the part that nobody expected and

7298
10:09:21,582 --> 10:09:24,376
which the narrator has left until now.

7299
10:09:24,776 --> 10:09:30,558
He was one hundred and sixty-nine years old. He did
not need a ship to survive vacuum,

7300
10:09:30,578 --> 10:09:36,699
could function at temperatures that destroy equipment,
and had a body that had been rebuilt

7301
10:09:36,719 --> 10:09:42,434
from the original strain in a room under a house in
Pennsylvania in 2062 and that had

7302
10:09:42,454 --> 10:09:45,066
no established upper limit on anything.

7303
10:09:45,466 --> 10:09:51,369
He served as a boarding specialist, under the
command of officers a hundred and thirty

7304
10:09:51,389 --> 10:09:55,985
years younger than him, in a unit of
eleven people, for nine years.

7305
10:09:56,385 --> 10:10:03,407
The narrator wants to state why, because four
hundred historians have got it wrong and

7306
10:10:03,427 --> 10:10:10,696
the answer is in a conversation he had with Evelyn
Marsh in 2196 that she published after

7307
10:10:10,716 --> 10:10:11,515
his death.

7308
10:10:12,034 --> 10:10:13,205
You could be running this.

7309
10:10:13,604 --> 10:10:20,017
I am running an eight-person boarding team on a hull
with a failed drive and I am extremely

7310
10:10:20,037 --> 10:10:20,794
good at it.

7311
10:10:21,195 --> 10:10:25,205
That is not an answer and we are both a
hundred and seventy years old.

7312
10:10:26,044 --> 10:10:32,606
(very soft) In a hundred and seventy years I have
never once been in a room where somebody

7313
10:10:32,626 --> 10:10:36,774
could tell me to do something, and
mean it, and be right.

7314
10:10:37,055 --> 10:10:44,780
Lieutenant Adeyemi-Vance is twenty-nine years old.
She is the great-great-granddaughter

7315
10:10:44,800 --> 10:10:52,348
of a woman who argued with me about money for
thirty-two years. She tells me where to

7316
10:10:52,368 --> 10:11:00,450
stand, and when to go, and twice she has told me I was
wrong, and she was right both times,

7317
10:11:00,470 --> 10:11:05,525
and I have obeyed her eleven hundred
times in four years.

7318
10:11:05,805 --> 10:11:12,611
(very cold) Do you understand what that is worth to
me? I have bought cities. I could

7319
10:11:12,631 --> 10:11:13,655
not buy that.

7320
10:11:14,055 --> 10:11:21,725
On the fourth of November 2210 an eight-person
boarding team took the interior of a Myriad

7321
10:11:21,745 --> 10:11:28,987
mass for the first time, and four of them came
back, and Albert Wesker carried two of

7322
10:11:29,007 --> 10:11:29,415
them.

7323
10:11:29,815 --> 10:11:35,735
What they brought back was the thing that ended the
war, and it is not what anybody expected,

7324
10:11:35,755 --> 10:11:40,079
and the narrator will describe it as
carefully as the record allows.

7325
10:11:40,479 --> 10:11:46,609
They found no command structure. They found no
individuals. What they found, in a chamber

7326
10:11:46,629 --> 10:11:52,553
four kilometres inside a body of four hundred
trillion, was a *memory*: a structure of

7327
10:11:52,573 --> 10:11:58,703
accreted mineral and tissue, nine hundred thousand
years old, in which the entire history

7328
10:11:58,723 --> 10:12:04,716
of everything the Myriad had ever eaten was
recorded, in order, in detail, with nothing

7329
10:12:04,736 --> 10:12:05,269
missing.

7330
10:12:05,668 --> 10:12:12,049
Eleven hundred species. Four hundred trillion
bodies' worth of experience. Nine hundred

7331
10:12:12,069 --> 10:12:13,153
thousand years.

7332
10:12:13,553 --> 10:12:19,269
It is the largest archive in the known volume of
space, and it belongs to a thing that

7333
10:12:19,289 --> 10:12:24,673
has never once used it for anything, because
there is nobody in there to read it.

7334
10:12:25,623 --> 10:12:29,073
Dr. Evelyn Marsh spent
twenty-six years on it.

7335
10:12:29,472 --> 10:12:36,828
Her conclusion, published in 2221 and never seriously
challenged, is four sentences, and

7336
10:12:36,848 --> 10:12:41,103
it is the most disturbing document
in this account.

7337
10:12:41,623 --> 10:12:48,250
The Myriad is not hostile. It is not anything. It is a
growth process with a perfect memory

7338
10:12:48,270 --> 10:12:51,172
and no capacity whatsoever to act on it.

7339
10:12:51,452 --> 10:12:57,375
Every species it has consumed is preserved in it, in
full, and none of them are alive,

7340
10:12:57,395 --> 10:13:00,762
and the structure has no
mechanism for retrieval.

7341
10:13:01,041 --> 10:13:06,699
It has been carrying eleven hundred civilisations
for nine hundred thousand years the

7342
10:13:06,719 --> 10:13:08,637
way a glacier carries a rock.

7343
10:13:08,916 --> 10:13:14,155
(very slow) I have spent my life making things that
do not die. This is what that looks

7344
10:13:14,175 --> 10:13:15,666
like when nobody is home.

7345
10:13:16,066 --> 10:13:20,696
The narrator would like one scene from the nine
years, and it is not a battle.

7346
10:13:21,097 --> 10:13:26,922
Lieutenant Adaeze Adeyemi-Vance was twenty-nine
years old and had eleven people under

7347
10:13:26,942 --> 10:13:32,837
her, one of whom was two hundred and eighty-four and
had founded the company that made

7348
10:13:32,857 --> 10:13:38,477
her ship, her suit, the medicine in her blood and
the city her mother was born in.

7349
10:13:38,877 --> 10:13:43,842
Her pre-mission briefings are on the record
because everything on a carrier is.

7350
10:13:44,362 --> 10:13:49,192
(radio) — and Wesker, you're on the left-hand
breach with Oyelaran. Not the right.

7351
10:13:49,591 --> 10:13:55,730
The right-hand approach is eleven metres shorter and
the mass density reading suggests

7352
10:13:55,750 --> 10:13:55,801
—

7353
10:13:56,201 --> 10:14:00,932
(radio) The mass density reading is four hours old
and I've got a fresher one that says

7354
10:14:00,952 --> 10:14:03,772
there's a plenum behind that wall.
Left-hand breach.

7355
10:14:04,502 --> 10:14:06,892
Left-hand breach, Lieutenant.

7356
10:14:07,291 --> 10:14:12,956
The Red Queen's log — she logged the boarding
actions in full, at his own request, from

7357
10:14:12,976 --> 10:14:18,836
2202 — records that he said *Lieutenant* eleven
hundred and forty-one times in nine years,

7358
10:14:18,856 --> 10:14:24,585
that he was overruled by her on four occasions of
tactical substance, that she was right

7359
10:14:24,605 --> 10:14:30,204
on all four, and that on the last of them the plenum
behind the right-hand wall killed

7360
10:14:30,224 --> 10:14:35,562
two of her people and would have killed four if he
had been where he wanted to be.

7361
10:14:35,961 --> 10:14:43,730
Adaeze Adeyemi-Vance retired as a commodore in 2241
and never once gave an interview about

7362
10:14:43,750 --> 10:14:51,260
him. Asked, in 2249, by a historian who had tracked
her down on a colony world, what he

7363
10:14:51,280 --> 10:14:58,703
had been like to command, she gave an answer of
twenty-four words that is the epigraph

7364
10:14:58,723 --> 10:15:00,606
of four hundred books.

7365
10:15:01,127 --> 10:15:04,857
He did what he was told, faster than
anyone, and never sulked.

7366
10:15:05,887 --> 10:15:14,109
Event: first boarding. Team of eight, four returned.
One hundred and forty-one personal

7367
10:15:14,129 --> 10:15:20,837
engagements. Nine thousand four hundred
Myriad bodies destroyed by you.

7368
10:15:21,867 --> 10:15:24,457
